// Credential rotation from the command line (SPEC 26):
//
//   symbolon device vault login DIR NAME ORIGIN USERNAME
//       the PIN, then the password, on stdin: a legacy login (fields name,
//       username, origin, current)
//   symbolon device rotate DIR NAME BUNDLE REPOSITORY [CHROMIUM] [--share ID]
//       the PIN on stdin (with --share, a login in that shared folder): the two-phase change of the login's password
//       (SPEC 26.3) by a signed, logged recipe (SPEC 26.4) in headless
//       Chromium
//
// The vault holds a password the site accepts at every moment: Prepare
// writes current and pending and publishes the vault (the relay copy is
// what every other device reads) before the browser changes anything;
// Verify signs in with pending, then with current, each in a fresh browser
// context, and writes the outcome; neither working leaves both, marked
// unresolved. A run that finds the item pending resumes at Verify. The
// item carries the rotation lease (field "lease": holder party and expiry)
// and the failed sign-ins (field "fails": times), counted across devices
// because they live in the vault.

